From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-RC1-011CI
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: synchronize RG35XX bitmap raster with MIDP font metrics

CH device evidence confirms glyphs are visible and readable, but text layers can
overlap normal view text. The fallback renderer still used a fixed 8x12 raster
while anchors/layout use Font.stringWidth()/getHeight(). Make the raster use the
same active Font metrics so visual pixels, clipping and MIDP layout share one
width/height contract.

--- a/src/org/recompile/mobile/PlatformGraphics.java
+++ b/src/org/recompile/mobile/PlatformGraphics.java
@@ -856,12 +856,13 @@
 			if(RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive() && !Mobile.isDoJa)
 			{
-				final int bitmapWidth = RG35XXBitmapText.width(str);
-				if(bitmapWidth > 0)
+				final int bitmapWidth = RG35XXBitmapText.width(str, font);
+				final int bitmapHeight = RG35XXBitmapText.height(font);
+				if(bitmapWidth > 0 && bitmapHeight > 0)
 				{
-					final int[] raster = RG35XXBitmapText.render(str, getColor());
+					final int[] raster = RG35XXBitmapText.render(str, getColor(), font);
 					drawRGB(raster, 0, bitmapWidth, x, y - ascent,
-						bitmapWidth, RG35XXBitmapText.CELL_HEIGHT, true);
+						bitmapWidth, bitmapHeight, true);
 				}
 			}
 			else
